<header>
  <p class="eyebrow">Andes Technology &middot; integration plan</p>
  <h1>AndeSim on FastSim</h1>
  <p class="lede">AndeSim runs its three modes by launching processes and passing a file between them. FastSim already owns the mechanism that replaces all of it: one set of modules, one address map, and a Lua file per platform. This is what the port means, what it deletes, and the order to do it in.</p>
  <p class="meta">Read from source, 2026-09-11 &middot; andesim &middot; fastsim &middot; vsim_andesim</p>
</header>

<section>
  <h2 class="sec-head">The goal</h2>
  <div class="out">
    <div>All three AndeSim modes &mdash; <b>fast</b>, <b>cycle</b>, <b>hybrid</b> &mdash; run on FastSim's existing mechanism: greenlib's <code>ModuleFactory</code>, a Lua platform file, and CCI parameters.</div>
    <div>The devices are shared because <b>there is only one set of them</b>. Not two implementations kept in step &mdash; one <code>router</code>, one <code>gs_memory</code>, one <code>SimControl</code>, reached by whichever CPU is running.</div>
    <div>The user-facing behaviour does not change. <code>andesim run --mode hybrid kernel.c</code> still prints one cycle count.</div>
  </div>
</section>

